Z||000000||PearlBlueSoul||11-28-2000||03:14 AM||||Hey!  just wanted to say wassup n all.  No hard feelings n stuff, cuz we all are a tad biased towards our respective cars.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  hehe. I know I sure am.<P>Just a question from me to yall to start with I guess...What type of driving to you guys like more?  Straights, or curves?  Cuz I was wondering who all had been up to a place called Deal's gap in North Carolina, sort of a biker place they know as the "Dragon".<P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR><A HREF="http://"http://www.atlantamr2s.com"" TARGET=_blank>www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://"http://www.geocities.com/darionscard"" TARGET=_blank>Pics of my car, "Heaven and Hell"</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg"> <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||11-28-2000||05:35 AM||||Hi! I must say that's a nice looking MR2, much nicer than some I see driving around where I live. About the type of driving I like: I like curved roads simply because the Fiero sticks to the road like glue! I don't like straights very much (like highways) because that brings out another thing a lot of Fieros suffer from: it tends to start floating at high speeds.<P>Anyways, stick around - maybe we can convince you to get a Fiero (too)...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||11-28-2000||09:55 AM||||I made the move from curvy hilly Northern California to straight flat Oklahoma, and I tell ya, I miss the curves!!! I love the feeling of that oversteer sliding the back out. Nothing better.||||reg||1
