Z||000008||PearlBlueSoul||11-28-2000||03:46 PM||||I'll give a hearty AMEN to that!  hehe.  Gotta say it's nice knowing very few things far side of italian supercars (the real things) can beat you in a corner...especially on a road like the dragon.  <P>The dragon, as it is commonly referred to by the biker group that rides it the most, is a streach of 11 miles, with 318 curves within those 11 miles.  BELIEVE ME, that place is the most BAD ASS road I've ever been on in my life.  I LOVe the curves, and 1 word only applies, APEX.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Once again, I thank you guys for the compliments on my car.  I really wish we could take to you guys so well as you have taken to me (least, I hope so).  Thanks, seriously.  <P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR><A HREF="http://"http://www.atlantamr2s.com"" TARGET=_blank>www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://"http://www.geocities.com/darionscard"" TARGET=_blank>Pics of my car, "Heaven and Hell"</A><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">  <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||1
