Z||000014||Standard||11-29-2000||03:05 AM||||Curves are fun!  I can't wait to lower my GT and put a sway bar on the rear...<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 153,000 miles and some busted up ground f/x  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redface.gif"> <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000015||PearlBlueSoul||11-29-2000||10:34 AM||||trust me, SWAY BARS HELP!!  I know the 86-88 model MR2s didn't have swaybars, but the 85 and 89 models did (for what reason, I don't know).  I got the Suspension Techniques adjustable sway bar kit, and I can tune it the way I want (oversteer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> or understeer), helped even day to day driving, and just made a large overall improvement in handling all around.  I did these seperately from my springs to so I can honestly say they do make a difference.<P>About the issues above:  <P>Yes, big guys can fit in them.  I'm 5"11, feel fine, with extra seat room left over to back up.  <BR>The gauges are in english, and they do read in MPH and KMH. <BR>I don't actually have the correct Toyota mechanic's manual, but from what I've heard the BGB (big green book, as we 2ers refer to it) is done well.  haven't had any problems with my Haynes manual, except its a lil vague sometimes (but they're all like that for the average mechanic).<BR>NO, they don't have cupholders!  Believe me, I realize this painful fact everytime I have to drive with a drink in my hand.  5 speed, in traffic, on barett parkway.  *ugh*<P>I'm at school right now so I gotta go, period is over!  hehe.  Onward!  <P>I'll be posting more tonight.<BR><P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">       <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||1
