Z||000028||DaRkLoRD||12-01-2000||01:06 AM||||I've heard a duke with quad resonator tips, and it didn't sound half bad... not as nice as the growl of a 2.8, but it wasn't anything like the coffeecan ricer sounds...<BR>I know of a duke with a cherry bomb exhaust, but I haven't had the chance to hear what it sounds like.<P>how about this.. if a Fiero has a pointy nose, and doesn't say "Formula" on the side, and it doesn't have black bumper pads on the front and the back.. it's likely a 4cyl.. but if it does have the black pads, it could be a V6 85SE.. and if it says Formula on the side.. well.. that one's pretty obvious.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>(fastest Fiero.. same power as a GT, but none of the extra stuff.. lighter weight)<P>or, you could just bite the bullet and buy the Fiero Spotters Guide, and be able to identify every model.. hehe<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
